      "description": "South Dakota Board of Regents Employment Opportunities | Adjunct - Instructor, Lecturer, or Senior Lecturer of Chemical and Biological Engineering Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct - Instructor, Lecturer, or Senior Lecturer of Chemical and Biological Engineering Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Logo Institution South Dakota Mines Working Title Adjunct - Instructor, Lecturer, or Senior Lecturer of Chemical and Biological Engineering Posting Number F01978P Department SDSMT-Karen M. Swindler Chemical and Biological Engineering Physical Location of Position (City) Rapid City Posting Text The Karen M. Swindler Department of Chemical and Biological Engineering at the South Dakota School of Mines & Technology invites applications for one or more part-time temporary Instructor, Lecturer, or Senior Lecturers to teach the Spring 2027 semester. This is a part-time, non-benefited position. The position may continue semester-by-semester, dependent upon performance, department need, funding and student enrollment. Successful applicants will have a master’s degree or an earned doctorate in Chemical Engineering or a related field by the time of appointment. Successful candidates will be required to teach core or elective chemical engineering courses, laboratories, or other courses as assigned. The Karen M. Swindler Department of Chemical and Biological Engineering ( CBE ) offers curriculum toward B.S., M.S., and Ph.D. degrees. Approximately 130 students are enrolled in the CBE undergraduate program and 30 students in the CBE graduate programs. For additional information regarding the CBE Department please visit our website, http://www.sdsmt.edu/ CBE / . Applications must be made online at https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu . South Dakota Mines is committed to recruiting and retaining a talented workforce and offers an excellent comprehensive b